# Project map (Godot 4.x)

- **Combat orchestrator:** `combat/CombatManager.gd` — Node with `combatants`, `event_queue`, signals. Keeps registration, `start()`, and thin `func` forwards. Loaded via `core/ResourcePaths.gd` → `COMBAT_MANAGER`.
- **Combat subsystems (preload from manager or call static):** `CombatProcessTick`, `CombatEventScheduler`, `CombatEventDispatch`, `CombatResolveAction`, `CombatEngagementResolver`, `CombatFormationFlow`, `CombatFormationSetup`, `CombatFormationEngagement` (line cohesion + posture; `CombatManager.engagement_state_changed`), `CombatIntrusionGeometry` (crash neighbor hold; future intruder distance/slots), `CombatDistanceBands`, `CombatCombatantsSnapshot` (UI rows), `CombatMedicalCoordination` (retry / parts under treatment), `AttackResolver`, `AvailableActionsBuilder`, `MedicalPhaseController`, etc. under `combat/`. Plan: `docs/ENGAGEMENT_LINE_COHESION_INTRUSION_PLAN.md`.
- **Tuning:** `combat/CombatConstants.gd` is large by design (single source of numeric constants).
- **Entities:** `core/CoreEntity.gd` plus `EntityMedical`, `EntityDamage`, `EntityWounds`, …
- **Battle UI:** `ui/BattleScene.gd`, `BattleUIUpdater.gd`, row/diagram builders under `ui/`.
- **Cross-plan implementation order:** `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_ORDER.md` (tiers 0–7). Engagement detail: `docs/ENGAGEMENT_LINE_COHESION_INTRUSION_PLAN.md`.

When adding behavior, extend the **smallest** existing module that owns that concern; avoid growing `CombatManager.gd` beyond orchestration and public API.
